{"ts_utc": "2026-05-12T15:56:06.172812Z", "run_id": "20260512_155524_rag_L3_B1_1dbf2f", "seq": 5, "event": "generation.completed", "payload": {"answer": "Parliament did not explicitly state its opinion on education policy, but it discussed issues related to the educational sector. The Hon Minister for Education was asked to come with a Statement on the matter, indicating that there were concerns about the educational system.\n\n[<chunk_id: 2fc50d4e2a88b6bf595eef06a7e0ea916fc876c9f0060a7868a860ee4fe7bf99:44>] mentions that the Committee on Education should engage the Hon Minister to do a detailed assessment of the subject matter.\n\n[<chunk_id: 09e40dc218eabe6140d3da9f41fa5089177303b29afff412bbf04b7939384856:52>] states that the Free Senior High School (FSHS) Programme was initiated by the previous Government, but its impact on education is a matter of concern.\n\n[<chunk_id: dfb854d2e036ec0d7e95b53e94c88bfc469f0184a4bc76853bf8d865ecd5540c:74>] mentions that the Hon Minister ensured that students got their schools of choice, but there were challenges with computer school placement.\n\n[<chunk_id: dfb854d2e036ec0d7e95b53e94c88bfc469f0184a4bc76853bf8d865ecd5540c:7>] states that the Hon Minister's own release admitted to challenges with school placements.", "answer_sha256": "c365feb799ba741470b21af4ccae6d42f0c84726551177d1585ee10381f99184"}, "prev_hash": "f409e33ea329e3e33ac71ce6a733b4b138a9edab916548bb06ba23691394ce31", "event_hash": "47d451ce62841ae6be7fd3895c20aba6fd4c264c7cfd2cf0c07f6151030931f5"}
